'''Ben Tennyson''', also known as '''Bad Ben''',{{Refn|[[:File:And Then There Were None Voice Credits (1).png]]|group = credits}}<ref name="And Then There Were None"/> is an alternate and evil version of [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Tennyson]].

==Appearance==
Bad Ben bears a very strong resemblance to Ben Prime, except he has black hair instead of brunette hair, which is natural.{{Refn|[[:File:Mad Ben Is Australian.PNG]]|group = DJW}} He also has mint green-colored eyes, shirt, and an [[Omnitrix]] of the same color. Plus his cargo pants are of a darker brown color and his shoes are black instead of green.

==Personality==
{{Quote|"Evil" is relative.|Bad Ben to [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]].<ref name="And Then There Were None" />}}
Bad Ben enjoys being bad; from small things such as intentionally withholding an explanation about the multiple Bens from [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] to maintain the latter's terror, to bigger things such as sadistically attacking and tormenting the good Bens.

Bad Ben also speaks slower than [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]].
Bad Ben has a twisted sense of humor, as he exclaimed to a crowd of shoppers upon suddenly poking his head out of a wall at them as [[Ghostfreak]], "Clean up on Aisle Ten!"
==History==
===Omniverse===
Bad Ben first appeared in ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', where he was among the evil Bens recruited by [[Eon]] and [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] from across the [[multiverse]] and brought to [[No Watch Timeline]] to wipe [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] out. Bad Ben was the first alternate Ben that No Watch Ben encountered. Bad Ben as [[Ghostfreak]] chased No Watch Ben through [[Bellwood (Classic)|town]], but No Watch Ben was saved by [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]]. Later, in [[Los Soledad]], Bad Ben was part of the fight between the good and evil Bens, as [[Gravattack]]. At the end of the episode, just like all the other Omnitrix wielders, he and his timeline were erased from space-time by the [[Chronosapien Time Bomb]].

In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', Bad Ben was brought back into existence when No Watch Ben used [[Clockwork]] to suck the Time Bomb's ripple back in. Later, he was chasing an Omnitrixless [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]] as [[Buzzshock (Classic)|Buzzshock]] along with [[Ultimate Echo Echo|Negative Ultimate Echo Echo]] and [[Mad Ben|Mad Ben]]. At the end of the episode, Bad Ben was sent back to his own reality by Clockwork.

==Powers and Abilities==
[[File:ATTWN (88).png|thumb|Fight Skills]]
Bad Ben displayed a few fighting skills against [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] in [[Human (Classic)|human]] form, explicitly stating that he had taken self-defense classes at some point.<ref name="And Then There Were None"/>

===Equipment===
[[File:ATTWN (91).png|thumb|Omnitrix]]
Like many of his other counterparts, Bad Ben possesses an [[Omnitrix (Bad Ben's Timeline)|Omnitrix]].

